four-hop traceroute — pc1 → dswa1 (10.1.0.2) → csw1 (10.0.0.45) → dswb2
(10.0.0.58) → srv1 — is intact and stable. srv1's startup configuration
confirms it is designed solely as a campus DNS resolver; it runs only named and
has never hosted a web server, file server, or any other application. TCP
attempts to ports 80, 22, 443, and 8080 all return an immediate "Connection
refused" (not a timeout), meaning packets reach srv1 unimpeded.

